@using GridGate.Launcher.Pages.Profile
@* How the owner of a Region Server or Connected Server gets the one-time link that lets them turn on two-factor (OwnerEnrolLinks). *@
<div id="two-factor-link" class="alert alert-info" role="status">
    <p>Your account lives on another grid, so two-factor sign-in can only be turned on from this computer.</p>
    <p>On the grid computer, run the launcher's <code>@TwoFactorModel.LinkCommand</code> and open the link it prints within 15 minutes, while signed in here.</p>
    <p>On Linux:<br><code>sudo runuser -u gridgate -- /opt/gridgate/dotnet/dotnet /opt/gridgate/launcher/GridGate.Launcher.dll @TwoFactorModel.LinkCommand</code></p>
    <p>On Windows, from an Administrator command prompt:<br><code>"C:\Program Files\GridGate\dotnet-&lt;version&gt;\dotnet.exe" "C:\Program Files\GridGate\launcher\GridGate.Launcher.dll" @TwoFactorModel.LinkCommand</code></p>
</div>
